  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member using SwiftHFR on an iPhone and an iPad, I want the app to actually use the iCloud-synced settings store, so that the preferences LOT-172 syncs follow my Apple ID.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- The iCloud key-value storage capability on the App ID and the `com.apple.developer.ubiquity-kvstore-identifier` entitlement in the app (ADR 0013 §9: a developer-portal action by the maintainer; no `.entitlements` file in `App/` yet)\n\n\n### Scope\n\nLOT-172 part 1 (#446) adds `SyncedSettingsStore` (HFRStorage) and `UbiquitousKeyValueStore`; nothing in `App/` uses them yet (the app builds `UserDefaultsSettingsStore()` directly).\n\n- Build one `SyncedSettingsStore(local: UserDefaultsSettingsStore(), cloud: UbiquitousKeyValueStore(), deviceState: FileSmallStorePersistence(fileURL: <Application Support, backed up, device-only>))` and inject it wherever a `SettingsStore` is built today.\n- Start `run()` once for the process; call `synchronize()` at launch and on foreground (ADR 0013 §4).\n- Surface `quotaViolations` and `deviceStateFailure` in the logs.\n- Order with the legacy import (LOT-067 / LOT-158, ADR 0013 §5): device import first, then the store.\n- Part 2 of LOT-172 (lists, reading positions) is wired the same way once merged.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-172 (#311, part 1 #446)\n- LOT-160 (#250): the iCloud key-value storage entitlement (ADR 0013 §9: a developer-portal action by the maintainer)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every `SettingsStore` the app builds is the synced one; no second `UserDefaultsSettingsStore` writes synced keys behind its back.\n- [ ] Two simulators (or an iPhone and an iPad) on one Apple ID see a synced setting change; a device-scoped one does not travel.\n- [ ] App tests with `InMemorySyncedKeyValueStore`; `App build + tests` green.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
